1
00:00:00,539 --> 00:00:03,739
(An activity on his bucket list he dreamed of doing since his 20s)

2
00:00:04,109 --> 00:00:06,779
(His last attempt at making his dream come true)

3
00:00:07,679 --> 00:00:08,948
(I'm walking...)

4
00:00:08,949 --> 00:00:10,449
(across the country.)

5
00:00:10,979 --> 00:00:12,719
(He had always been disappointed that he couldn't complete it.)

6
00:00:13,219 --> 00:00:15,319
(Then he had to say goodbye to his friend.)

7
00:00:16,019 --> 00:00:18,119
(He decided to give it a try again.)

8
00:00:18,419 --> 00:00:21,588
(Distance traveled)

9
00:00:21,589 --> 00:00:24,389
(Distance traveled: 421km)

10
00:00:25,199 --> 00:00:28,728
(17 days of traveling from Seoul to Gwangalli)

11
00:00:28,729 --> 00:00:30,268
(Current location)

12
00:00:30,269 --> 00:00:33,399
(On his last day, he only had 25km left.)

13
00:00:34,069 --> 00:00:36,209
(He was running on fumes at this point.)

14
00:00:36,309 --> 00:00:37,309
Hongga.

15
00:00:37,839 --> 00:00:39,738
- He startled me. What? - His forehead...

16
00:00:39,739 --> 00:00:41,308
Doesn't it look like a halo?

17
00:00:41,309 --> 00:00:42,909
(He had a walking buddy who was much like an angel.)

18
00:00:43,909 --> 00:00:45,318
(And he had another friend...)

19
00:00:45,319 --> 00:00:48,179
(keeping him company during his travel.)

20
00:00:49,949 --> 00:00:52,319
(When I looked at it, it gave me strength.)

21
00:00:52,889 --> 00:00:54,988
(His last step to finish the walk)

22
00:00:54,989 --> 00:00:55,989
(Let's go!)

23
00:00:56,359 --> 00:00:58,059
(This is such a luxury for us.)

24
00:00:58,929 --> 00:01:00,759
(This is the highlight of walking across the country.)

25
00:01:01,699 --> 00:01:03,329
(I need to use the restroom.)

26
00:01:03,769 --> 00:01:05,939
(It's on the border.)

27
00:01:06,469 --> 00:01:08,099
(Come on. It's the stairs again.)

28
00:01:08,439 --> 00:01:11,039
(The never-ending stairs)

29
00:01:11,369 --> 00:01:13,108
(Oh, my legs...)

30
00:01:13,109 --> 00:01:14,239
(Even my knees hurt.)

31
00:01:15,009 --> 00:01:16,879
(To make it worse, it began pouring down.)

32
00:01:17,449 --> 00:01:19,149
(Come on. What is that?)

33
00:01:20,019 --> 00:01:21,449
(It's not a hill. It's a mountain.)

34
00:01:22,319 --> 00:01:24,249
(Staggering)

35
00:01:25,259 --> 00:01:27,419
(Why did I ever decide to walk across the country?)

36
00:01:27,859 --> 00:01:30,859
(16 nights and 17 days, distance traveled: 432km)

37
00:01:32,929 --> 00:01:33,959
Okay.

38
00:01:34,859 --> 00:01:36,129
I made it all the way here.

39
00:01:37,369 --> 00:01:38,639
I made it all the way here.

40
00:01:39,769 --> 00:01:40,939
I can't let this...

41
00:01:42,169 --> 00:01:44,438
(Groaning)

42
00:01:44,439 --> 00:01:45,509
I'm almost there.

43
00:01:47,779 --> 00:01:50,378
It goes for all cars. If you take a break in first gear,

44
00:01:50,379 --> 00:01:51,848
it's hard to go up the hill.

45
00:01:51,849 --> 00:01:52,849
- Right. - That's...

46
00:01:52,850 --> 00:01:54,619
- They would roll back. - Yes, they'd roll backward.

47
00:01:58,559 --> 00:01:59,819
(Screaming)

48
00:02:00,519 --> 00:02:02,759
(Grunting)

49
00:02:03,359 --> 00:02:04,729
You can't do this alone.

50
00:02:04,989 --> 00:02:06,259
They got each other.

51
00:02:06,459 --> 00:02:07,829
He would've given up long ago if he were alone.

52
00:02:10,229 --> 00:02:11,268
Ta-da.

53
00:02:11,269 --> 00:02:13,339
(He finally reaches the top.)

54
00:02:14,639 --> 00:02:16,938
(Groaning)

55
00:02:16,939 --> 00:02:18,779
(Exhaling)

56
00:02:20,709 --> 00:02:23,549
(Spacing out)

57
00:02:24,949 --> 00:02:27,148
That's how I felt exactly when Baengnokdam came into view.

58
00:02:27,149 --> 00:02:29,948
(That's how I felt exactly when Baengnokdam came into view.)

59
00:02:29,949 --> 00:02:32,319
You're bringing up Mount Halla again?

60
00:02:32,419 --> 00:02:34,619
Let me explain. That was the toughest moment for me.

61
00:02:35,359 --> 00:02:36,529
You went there four years ago.

62
00:02:36,859 --> 00:02:38,488
- It was four years ago? - Yes.

63
00:02:38,489 --> 00:02:40,259
- Hyun Moo, then... - I mentioned it 40 times.

64
00:02:44,229 --> 00:02:47,099
(This is his 41st time mentioning his hike to Baengnokdam.)

65
00:02:47,939 --> 00:02:50,039
You're so cool. Happy New Year.

66
00:02:51,539 --> 00:02:54,039
(Baengnokdam is the best.)

67
00:02:54,909 --> 00:02:56,649
(Panting)

68
00:02:57,109 --> 00:02:58,148
Let's go.

69
00:02:58,149 --> 00:02:59,679
(They set out again after catching their breath.)

70
00:03:01,249 --> 00:03:03,118
(Gwangalli Beach, Busan)

71
00:03:03,119 --> 00:03:04,518
You're halfway there.

72
00:03:04,519 --> 00:03:06,919
(Distance traveled: 12km Distance remaining: 13km)

73
00:03:10,189 --> 00:03:11,489
Is it raining?

74
00:03:11,929 --> 00:03:13,129
I think it's hailing.

75
00:03:13,999 --> 00:03:16,268
Come on. Even the weather is killing me.

76
00:03:16,269 --> 00:03:17,299
How nice.

77
00:03:17,469 --> 00:03:19,869
(Clenching his teeth)

78
00:03:21,239 --> 00:03:23,609
(The storm is getting stronger.)

79
00:03:24,769 --> 00:03:26,779
(The two of them are getting soaked in the rain and the wind.)

80
00:03:28,239 --> 00:03:30,779
Oh, no. What a tough time they're having.

81
00:03:31,379 --> 00:03:35,049
(The bad weather is tiring him out little by little.)

82
00:03:36,089 --> 00:03:37,949
Actor Ku. I'm a fan.

83
00:03:39,019 --> 00:03:41,288
(Actor Ku. I'm a fan.)

84
00:03:41,289 --> 00:03:44,159
I saw you walking by earlier, so I bought this for you.

85
00:03:44,829 --> 00:03:46,028
I'm about to tear up now.

86
00:03:46,029 --> 00:03:48,099
- My gosh. I would tear up too. - I'd be so grateful too.

87
00:03:48,999 --> 00:03:50,268
I want to give you a hug.

88
00:03:50,269 --> 00:03:51,668
- But I'm wet. - I'm a huge fan.

89
00:03:51,669 --> 00:03:52,698
- Thank you. - I'll keep supporting you.

90
00:03:52,699 --> 00:03:53,738
- Have a good day. - Thank you.

91
00:03:53,739 --> 00:03:54,939
I'll enjoy this too.

92
00:03:56,139 --> 00:03:57,139
(Touched)

93
00:03:57,140 --> 00:03:58,169
- My gosh. - I'd be so grateful.

94
00:03:58,369 --> 00:03:59,608
He saw me from afar.

95
00:03:59,609 --> 00:04:01,038
- And he bought me coffee. - My gosh.

96
00:04:01,039 --> 00:04:02,849
- He followed you after buying it. - Yes, he did.

97
00:04:03,349 --> 00:04:04,809
- That's such a kind gesture. - That's so touching.

98
00:04:05,819 --> 00:04:06,849
I'm so grateful.

99
00:04:08,419 --> 00:04:09,849
Holding this coffee is keeping me warm.

100
00:04:10,189 --> 00:04:12,118
(Precious)

101
00:04:12,119 --> 00:04:13,189
I guess it was cold.

102
00:04:13,389 --> 00:04:14,389
You know what?

103
00:04:14,390 --> 00:04:16,059
You barely stand out in this episode.

104
00:04:17,529 --> 00:04:18,588
He's so eye-catching.

105
00:04:18,589 --> 00:04:20,559
(A scene-stealer)

106
00:04:21,959 --> 00:04:23,599
(Thanks to the warm coffee,)

107
00:04:24,569 --> 00:04:26,539
(the two of them continue walking.)

108
00:04:27,639 --> 00:04:29,639
We walked over 10km now, right?

109
00:04:30,439 --> 00:04:31,869
(Swinging)

110
00:04:31,939 --> 00:04:33,038
We walked 13.5km.

111
00:04:33,039 --> 00:04:34,379
You guys came a long way.

112
00:04:35,009 --> 00:04:36,378
We're past our halfway point.

113
00:04:36,379 --> 00:04:39,779
(Distance traveled: 13.5km Distance remaining: 11.5km)

114
00:04:39,919 --> 00:04:40,948
Seriously.

115
00:04:40,949 --> 00:04:41,988
(He's so close to completing his grand journey of 446km.)

116
00:04:41,989 --> 00:04:43,488
I'm so close.

117
00:04:43,489 --> 00:04:44,849
My gosh, 16 nights and 17 days.

118
00:04:45,519 --> 00:04:48,459
It must feel like it's been a month.

119
00:04:52,099 --> 00:04:53,499
(Struggling)

120
00:04:57,899 --> 00:04:59,439
(Groaning)

121
00:04:59,939 --> 00:05:02,039
(Limping)

122
00:05:02,669 --> 00:05:04,839
(It seems something's wrong with him.)

123
00:05:06,109 --> 00:05:10,709
(His face begins to stiffen.)

124
00:05:11,979 --> 00:05:14,248
(Sighing)

125
00:05:14,249 --> 00:05:15,849
Gosh, my calves are killing me.

126
00:05:17,849 --> 00:05:18,989
Come on.

127
00:05:21,419 --> 00:05:22,729
Oh, my back.

128
00:05:24,559 --> 00:05:26,929
(Worried)

129
00:05:28,399 --> 00:05:30,068
Okay. Let's keep going. We're very close.

130
00:05:30,069 --> 00:05:31,128
Okay.

131
00:05:31,129 --> 00:05:32,669
- We can do it. - We can do it.

132
00:05:33,969 --> 00:05:35,609
Getting this far wasn't easy.

133
00:05:35,739 --> 00:05:36,969
Right. It wasn't easy.

134
00:05:41,539 --> 00:05:43,479
To be honest, I felt really bad for Hongga.

135
00:05:44,509 --> 00:05:46,349
I couldn't keep up with his pace.

136
00:05:47,549 --> 00:05:48,578
My gosh.

137
00:05:48,579 --> 00:05:49,649
(Let me man up and keep going.)

138
00:05:53,889 --> 00:05:55,019
You're even clenching your teeth.

139
00:05:56,189 --> 00:05:58,228
It was really difficult for you to keep walking at that point.

140
00:05:58,229 --> 00:06:01,999
Didn't seeing cars speed by make you want to get in one?

141
00:06:02,169 --> 00:06:03,798
I didn't think about that.

142
00:06:03,799 --> 00:06:07,368
My goal was to walk 446km.

143
00:06:07,369 --> 00:06:10,109
If I were to get on the wheels even for 10m,

144
00:06:10,339 --> 00:06:12,478
it would make me feel my whole journey was fake.

145
00:06:12,479 --> 00:06:14,078
- It would negate the whole purpose. - It would.

146
00:06:14,079 --> 00:06:15,578
I bet you felt more like that since it was your last day.

147
00:06:15,579 --> 00:06:17,278
That's why when people saw me on the street,

148
00:06:17,279 --> 00:06:19,479
they asked me if I wanted a ride.

149
00:06:19,549 --> 00:06:21,418
- A lot of people offered. - Really?

150
00:06:21,419 --> 00:06:23,148
If I took the offer, this would be meaningless.

151
00:06:23,149 --> 00:06:25,558
- The whole thing would be fake. - That's right. So I said no.

152
00:06:25,559 --> 00:06:28,118
It was a challenge against yourself and a promise at the same time.

153
00:06:28,119 --> 00:06:29,189
Right.

154
00:06:29,529 --> 00:06:30,788
Hey, it's raining quite a lot.

155
00:06:30,789 --> 00:06:32,128
- We should take shelter... - Yes.

156
00:06:32,129 --> 00:06:34,959
- under a roof when we see one. - Okay.

157
00:06:35,199 --> 00:06:37,969
- I need to check on my feet too. - Okay.

158
00:06:38,769 --> 00:06:40,399
It must've been harder since the weather was bad.

159
00:06:41,369 --> 00:06:43,969
When my shoes got wet, my feet kept sliding in them.

160
00:06:44,439 --> 00:06:45,979
That would cause more blisters.

161
00:06:47,839 --> 00:06:50,779
Right here. There's a gazebo.

162
00:06:51,079 --> 00:06:53,948
Hey. My gosh. That's the perfect spot.

163
00:06:53,949 --> 00:06:55,689
- Let's take a test here. - I love it.

164
00:06:56,649 --> 00:06:57,888
(Regrouping for a moment to avoid the rain)

165
00:06:57,889 --> 00:06:59,159
Wait, it's a cat.

166
00:07:01,789 --> 00:07:03,529
(Groaning)

167
00:07:04,929 --> 00:07:06,199
How can he not grunt?

168
00:07:06,929 --> 00:07:08,229
Lie down for a bit.

169
00:07:09,269 --> 00:07:10,468
I should check on them.

170
00:07:10,469 --> 00:07:11,899
Putting on wet shoes again would be tough.

171
00:07:15,969 --> 00:07:17,238
I don't think you can ever throw out those shoes.

172
00:07:17,239 --> 00:07:18,909
- Never. - Right?

173
00:07:19,809 --> 00:07:21,138
(Lying down)

174
00:07:21,139 --> 00:07:22,279
My goodness.

175
00:07:23,179 --> 00:07:25,779
Oh, my. Lying down on the gazebo...

176
00:07:31,419 --> 00:07:33,459
Shouldn't we have reached Gwangalli at this rate?

177
00:07:34,589 --> 00:07:36,558
My calves are killing me.

178
00:07:36,559 --> 00:07:38,789
(The journey of 446km doesn't seem to end.)

179
00:07:41,329 --> 00:07:42,999
Check on your toes. See if they're okay.

180
00:07:44,099 --> 00:07:45,398
He barely talked on the way.

181
00:07:45,399 --> 00:07:47,139
- I started to get worried. Yes. - It made you worry.

182
00:07:49,609 --> 00:07:50,739
Oh, no.

183
00:07:50,869 --> 00:07:51,909
What's wrong?

184
00:07:52,009 --> 00:07:53,078
Right here too.

185
00:07:53,079 --> 00:07:55,278
(His blistered foot got soaked in the rain.)

186
00:07:55,279 --> 00:07:57,179
- My gosh. - He stuck a thread in there.

187
00:07:57,609 --> 00:07:59,319
(Shutting his eyes)

188
00:07:59,719 --> 00:08:01,519
Hey. Doesn't that hurt?

189
00:08:04,349 --> 00:08:07,218
Hongga's feet were in worse shape than mine.

190
00:08:07,219 --> 00:08:09,259
- But he didn't say a thing. - Right.

191
00:08:09,389 --> 00:08:11,529
The blister kept getting popped inside his shoe.

192
00:08:11,789 --> 00:08:12,898
That guy, Hongga, is amazing.

193
00:08:12,899 --> 00:08:14,259
- He didn't show it at all. - Right.

194
00:08:14,699 --> 00:08:16,598
- He's such a cool guy. - He didn't show it.

195
00:08:16,599 --> 00:08:18,169
He's an amazing guy.

196
00:08:18,399 --> 00:08:19,569
My foot...

197
00:08:21,899 --> 00:08:24,268
(Looking clean)

198
00:08:24,269 --> 00:08:25,439
It looks fine.

199
00:08:26,479 --> 00:08:28,408
My body itself is super strong.

200
00:08:28,409 --> 00:08:29,409
(Laughing)

201
00:08:29,410 --> 00:08:31,579
Hey. I practically have baby feet.

202
00:08:31,949 --> 00:08:34,549
I have the feet of an infant. I have baby feet.

203
00:08:35,249 --> 00:08:38,348
So your frame is fine. But the engine must be rotting.

204
00:08:38,349 --> 00:08:40,919
Comparing it to a car... Hey, it's not rotting.

205
00:08:41,789 --> 00:08:44,659
(Rustling)

206
00:08:46,399 --> 00:08:48,658
Hey, you're addicted. You finished the whole bag of seasoned salt.

207
00:08:48,659 --> 00:08:50,199
That was a fresh bag.

208
00:08:50,329 --> 00:08:51,728
- No, this is... - Hey.

209
00:08:51,729 --> 00:08:53,138
(Grabbing)

210
00:08:53,139 --> 00:08:56,109
That's all you have left from this 250g bag. This is crazy.

211
00:08:57,269 --> 00:08:59,608
That's why you can't sleep and keep going to the bathroom at night.

212
00:08:59,609 --> 00:09:01,909
I'm telling you. This is very effective.

213
00:09:03,349 --> 00:09:04,349
(Shaking)

214
00:09:04,350 --> 00:09:05,549
Hey.

215
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:07,378
- Hey. - Oh, no. Sir.

216
00:09:07,379 --> 00:09:08,478
Sir.

217
00:09:08,479 --> 00:09:10,049
(Gulping it down)

218
00:09:10,319 --> 00:09:11,748
I feel so refreshed with some salt.

219
00:09:11,749 --> 00:09:13,059
That's true, though.

220
00:09:13,319 --> 00:09:15,259
Some salt definitely refreshed you.

221
00:09:15,359 --> 00:09:16,959
Hey, let me take some too.

222
00:09:17,689 --> 00:09:20,599
(Let me try some salt too.)

223
00:09:21,159 --> 00:09:22,769
It's like taking a tequila shot.

224
00:09:25,399 --> 00:09:26,669
You took too much.

225
00:09:29,239 --> 00:09:31,509
Hear me out. The salt hits you so aggressively.

226
00:09:32,439 --> 00:09:33,778
I get why you keep taking it.

227
00:09:33,779 --> 00:09:35,479
I almost finished it.

228
00:09:35,609 --> 00:09:37,478
Right. You almost finished it.

229
00:09:37,479 --> 00:09:40,278
(He finished a whole bag of seasoned salt.)

230
00:09:40,279 --> 00:09:42,818
- Is it different salt? - A lot of people participating...

231
00:09:42,819 --> 00:09:44,188
in triathlons and marathons...

232
00:09:44,189 --> 00:09:45,589
- do eat salt. - People eat salt during marathons.

233
00:09:45,659 --> 00:09:48,758
- But they don't take seasoned salt. - Here's why.

234
00:09:48,759 --> 00:09:51,629
We both have this in common. We have the palate of a kid.

235
00:09:51,989 --> 00:09:53,199
So it has to be tasty.

236
00:09:53,629 --> 00:09:55,869
(Laughing)

237
00:09:56,729 --> 00:09:57,828
Okay.

238
00:09:57,829 --> 00:09:58,898
(After a seasoned-salt refresher...)

239
00:09:58,899 --> 00:09:59,999
Are your legs okay?

240
00:10:00,169 --> 00:10:01,799
Let's get going. We're very close.

241
00:10:01,899 --> 00:10:02,969
Yes.

242
00:10:04,909 --> 00:10:06,408
(They set out again with the energy from seasoned salt.)

243
00:10:06,409 --> 00:10:07,779
My gosh, this is so nice.

244
00:10:09,479 --> 00:10:10,749
We're getting so close.

245
00:10:12,879 --> 00:10:15,449
(This is great.)

246
00:10:16,319 --> 00:10:17,588
Let's keep going.

247
00:10:17,589 --> 00:10:18,918
(After a short break...)

248
00:10:18,919 --> 00:10:19,988
Let's keep going.

249
00:10:19,989 --> 00:10:22,159
- That was a great energy boost. - We're very close.

250
00:10:23,989 --> 00:10:26,199
(Walking over a puddle)

251
00:10:26,899 --> 00:10:29,968
After a trip like that, I bet you'd know all the regions by heart.

252
00:10:29,969 --> 00:10:30,969
Gosh, no. I didn't even know...

253
00:10:30,970 --> 00:10:32,738
- where I was going, to be honest. - Really? You can't even remember?

254
00:10:32,739 --> 00:10:35,269
- I was just walking mindlessly. - Because it was really tough?

255
00:10:36,369 --> 00:10:39,379
I'm feeling a bit more energy now that we're getting close.

256
00:10:40,579 --> 00:10:43,749
Stay strong, Power Ku

257
00:10:45,049 --> 00:10:46,249
Let's keep at it.

258
00:10:47,019 --> 00:10:49,149
(Frowning)

259
00:10:50,849 --> 00:10:51,888
What happened?

260
00:10:51,889 --> 00:10:53,459
(Looking fatigued)

261
00:10:53,889 --> 00:10:55,659
Gosh, why is it raining so much? Oh, no.

262
00:10:56,729 --> 00:10:58,729
- Hey, it's raining way too hard. - Oh, my.

263
00:10:58,789 --> 00:11:00,259
It's pouring down.

264
00:11:01,159 --> 00:11:02,769
All right. Let's keep a positive mindset.

265
00:11:02,969 --> 00:11:03,969
Okay.

266
00:11:04,869 --> 00:11:06,799
Let's only think about Gwangalli. Come on.

267
00:11:07,499 --> 00:11:09,038
It's raining too hard.

268
00:11:09,039 --> 00:11:10,408
And it's super windy too.

269
00:11:10,409 --> 00:11:12,109
(They can't keep their eyes open due to the strong wind and rain.)

270
00:11:13,739 --> 00:11:15,539
- For goodness' sake. - My goodness.

271
00:11:17,149 --> 00:11:19,549
My gosh. It's windy and raining.

272
00:11:20,519 --> 00:11:21,719
Oh, my. I guess...

273
00:11:22,689 --> 00:11:25,959
this year will be full of happy occasions.

274
00:11:26,319 --> 00:11:28,489
Actually, if we had good weather today,

275
00:11:28,989 --> 00:11:30,288
it wouldn't be that memorable.

276
00:11:30,289 --> 00:11:32,659
- Right. That will be memorable. - And...

277
00:11:32,959 --> 00:11:35,129
- Hard times are more memorable. - That's right.

278
00:11:37,099 --> 00:11:40,099
(He keeps telling himself positive things.)

279
00:11:41,169 --> 00:11:45,009
(Trudging along)

280
00:11:48,079 --> 00:11:49,149
He's limping.

281
00:11:51,009 --> 00:11:54,519
(Despite his positive mindset, his legs are tired.)

282
00:11:55,349 --> 00:11:56,589
(Glancing)

283
00:11:56,949 --> 00:11:59,619
- How long do we have left? - From here?

284
00:12:00,489 --> 00:12:02,089
- About 8.5km. - About 8.5km.

285
00:12:02,259 --> 00:12:03,828
Then we have only two hours to go.

286
00:12:03,829 --> 00:12:05,189
(Distance traveled: 16.5km Distance remaining: 8.5km)

287
00:12:05,829 --> 00:12:09,799
(16 nights, 17 days, distance traveled: 437.5km)

288
00:12:11,729 --> 00:12:13,298
My gosh. Seriously.

289
00:12:13,299 --> 00:12:16,239
- Gosh, the backpack must be heavy. - It must be.

290
00:12:16,639 --> 00:12:19,278
Actually, walking 25km in 1 day isn't that bad...

291
00:12:19,279 --> 00:12:20,709
out of all the days we walked so far.

292
00:12:20,839 --> 00:12:22,178
- But you did that day after day. - Right.

293
00:12:22,179 --> 00:12:24,578
- That's right. - Going to a supermarket is tough...

294
00:12:24,579 --> 00:12:26,078
- when it rains that hard. - Right.

295
00:12:26,079 --> 00:12:28,079
I couldn't see ahead and because of the wind,

296
00:12:28,279 --> 00:12:30,289
the resistance made it harder to walk.

297
00:12:32,019 --> 00:12:35,219
(My gosh, this isn't easy.)

298
00:12:36,329 --> 00:12:37,459
Lean over there.

299
00:12:39,329 --> 00:12:41,928
(Leaning against the telephone pole)

300
00:12:41,929 --> 00:12:42,998
This is crazy.

301
00:12:42,999 --> 00:12:44,069
(Leaning against the telephone pole)

302
00:12:44,799 --> 00:12:48,169
(They lean their body while waiting for the signal.)

303
00:12:49,139 --> 00:12:51,709
You must want to lean on anything you see.

304
00:12:52,539 --> 00:12:54,208
I rarely lean on the poles when it rains.

305
00:12:54,209 --> 00:12:55,709
- Right. - Because of electric shocks.

306
00:12:57,749 --> 00:12:59,818
I hate jeopardizing my safety.

307
00:12:59,819 --> 00:13:01,519
- Just in case? - Just in case.

308
00:13:02,079 --> 00:13:03,689
But I didn't care about that then.

309
00:13:05,049 --> 00:13:08,859
(Walking through the heavy rain pouring down on him)

310
00:13:09,989 --> 00:13:11,588
(They force themselves to keep walking.)

311
00:13:11,589 --> 00:13:13,098
I don't think I can do that.

312
00:13:13,099 --> 00:13:14,559
(Amazed)

313
00:13:15,869 --> 00:13:16,898
I want to rest.

314
00:13:16,899 --> 00:13:18,299
Gosh, we made it to Beomil-dong.

315
00:13:20,799 --> 00:13:21,799
- Gosh. - Are you almost there?

316
00:13:21,999 --> 00:13:23,409
We're here. We're so close to finishing it.

317
00:13:25,369 --> 00:13:27,678
(Let's keep walking a little bit more.)

318
00:13:27,679 --> 00:13:29,779
(Closing his eyes)

319
00:13:35,889 --> 00:13:37,149
You guys stopped talking.

320
00:13:37,449 --> 00:13:39,018
We just sat down without saying a thing.

321
00:13:39,019 --> 00:13:40,059
(They quietly plop down on the bench.)

322
00:13:41,889 --> 00:13:45,228
(They're walking without saying a thing to each other.)

323
00:13:45,229 --> 00:13:46,258
(Then they rest for a bit.)

324
00:13:46,259 --> 00:13:47,528
- Oh, no. - My gosh.

325
00:13:47,529 --> 00:13:48,629
(Heartbroken)

326
00:13:49,769 --> 00:13:51,068
My gosh. Come on.

327
00:13:51,069 --> 00:13:53,069
(When on earth will we get to finish this journey?)

328
00:13:53,569 --> 00:13:54,968
There's a pattern.

329
00:13:54,969 --> 00:13:58,168
We start off by telling each other supportive things. "Good job."

330
00:13:58,169 --> 00:14:00,079
"Let's go there tomorrow."

331
00:14:00,509 --> 00:14:02,948
But the thing is, after the third day,

332
00:14:02,949 --> 00:14:04,679
- we didn't have much to talk about. - Right.

333
00:14:05,309 --> 00:14:07,178
It took a toll on us physically.

334
00:14:07,179 --> 00:14:08,318
(The harder it got, the quieter they got.)

335
00:14:08,319 --> 00:14:11,718
Because of that, when it got quiet, I had all kinds of thoughts.

336
00:14:11,719 --> 00:14:13,319
One of the thoughts would be,

337
00:14:13,959 --> 00:14:16,159
"What's the point of doing this?"

338
00:14:16,629 --> 00:14:17,958
"No one will give me credit for it."

339
00:14:17,959 --> 00:14:19,398
"This won't get me an award or anything."

340
00:14:19,399 --> 00:14:20,498
(This won't get me an award or anything.)

341
00:14:20,499 --> 00:14:23,298
These thoughts kept bothering me and made me want to give up.

342
00:14:23,299 --> 00:14:25,099
- You had a lot on your mind. - But...

343
00:14:25,429 --> 00:14:26,769
the hardest moment for me was...

344
00:14:27,439 --> 00:14:28,799
"Why am I so weak?"

345
00:14:28,969 --> 00:14:31,409
"I used to be so positive. Why am I so weak-minded?"

346
00:14:31,739 --> 00:14:33,679
Despite all that, I didn't give up...

347
00:14:34,439 --> 00:14:35,678
because it might haunt me.

348
00:14:35,679 --> 00:14:39,149
The failed attempt in my 20s kept haunting me.

349
00:14:39,779 --> 00:14:41,578
I couldn't finish the walk...

350
00:14:41,579 --> 00:14:42,949
because the bottoms of my feet were killing me.

351
00:14:43,089 --> 00:14:44,389
Whenever bad things happened to me,

352
00:14:44,519 --> 00:14:46,688
I thought, "That makes sense. I gave up..."

353
00:14:46,689 --> 00:14:48,389
"so easily that time."

354
00:14:48,719 --> 00:14:51,258
"So whenever things got tough,"

355
00:14:51,259 --> 00:14:54,099
"I just wanted to give up." I thought about giving up first.

356
00:14:54,359 --> 00:14:56,928
I was trying to put an end to that with this journey.

357
00:14:56,929 --> 00:14:58,099
That was why.

358
00:14:58,299 --> 00:14:59,938
That pushed me to challenge myself.

359
00:14:59,939 --> 00:15:01,298
- This journey had several purposes. - Yes.

360
00:15:01,299 --> 00:15:02,869
I wanted to achieve a lot with this journey.

361
00:15:04,469 --> 00:15:08,009
(That's why I can't give up.)

362
00:15:08,809 --> 00:15:11,148
I thought, "Let's take one step at a time."

363
00:15:11,149 --> 00:15:13,119
(He simply continues walking one step at a time.)

364
00:15:14,579 --> 00:15:18,519
I kept trying to be grateful.

365
00:15:20,519 --> 00:15:22,929
(He remembered...)

366
00:15:23,889 --> 00:15:26,599
(many grateful moments from his 17-day journey.)

367
00:15:27,559 --> 00:15:29,799
(Like a mom...)

368
00:15:30,899 --> 00:15:32,998
(and a friend, they gave him strength to keep going.)

369
00:15:32,999 --> 00:15:34,568
- I'm about to tear up now. - Thank you.

370
00:15:34,569 --> 00:15:35,569
(Thank you.)

371
00:15:36,609 --> 00:15:38,869
(And...)

372
00:15:39,679 --> 00:15:44,279
(he also had a partner who walked by his side.)

373
00:15:45,909 --> 00:15:49,549
(Out of gratitude for everyone's support...)

374
00:15:49,889 --> 00:15:50,919
Gosh, it's cold.

375
00:15:51,389 --> 00:15:53,118
- I just kept going. I just did it. - Right.

376
00:15:53,119 --> 00:15:54,359
- That's the spirit. - Yes.

377
00:15:56,689 --> 00:15:57,689
(Breathing out)

378
00:15:59,629 --> 00:16:01,559
I can see my breath when it's April now.

379
00:16:02,229 --> 00:16:03,329
It was 8°C that day.

380
00:16:03,569 --> 00:16:05,298
- The temperature dropped a lot. - It must've been freezing.

381
00:16:05,299 --> 00:16:07,268
- It was cold. - You kept walking in the rain.

382
00:16:07,269 --> 00:16:08,599
- We kept walking in the rain. - Yes.

383
00:16:10,239 --> 00:16:11,368
(Gwangalli Beach)

384
00:16:11,369 --> 00:16:15,109
(Distance traveled: 20.5km Distance remaining: 4.5km)

385
00:16:17,209 --> 00:16:19,249
(Glancing)

386
00:16:19,849 --> 00:16:22,179
Hey, look.

387
00:16:24,289 --> 00:16:27,519
(He spots something and goes straight to it.)

388
00:16:27,919 --> 00:16:28,959
Hello.

389
00:16:29,089 --> 00:16:30,688
- Can I get a haircut? - Sure.

390
00:16:30,689 --> 00:16:32,059
- What? - That was random.

391
00:16:33,129 --> 00:16:35,058
I'm sorry. But we're wet from the rain.

392
00:16:35,059 --> 00:16:37,068
- Sure. It's okay. - Okay.

393
00:16:37,069 --> 00:16:38,099
That was so random.

394
00:16:38,799 --> 00:16:41,039
It's the same for me and Hongga.

395
00:16:41,469 --> 00:16:43,139
We wanted to reset...

396
00:16:44,069 --> 00:16:45,509
our mindset.

397
00:16:45,739 --> 00:16:48,479
I wanted to change everything and start fresh.

398
00:16:49,009 --> 00:16:51,308
I was sweating so much when I was walking.

399
00:16:51,309 --> 00:16:53,279
We talked about it and decided to get a haircut...

400
00:16:53,449 --> 00:16:55,979
toward the end when we were close to finishing it.

401
00:16:56,449 --> 00:16:58,548
The way you embrace the end is really important.

402
00:16:58,549 --> 00:17:00,918
- Yes. That's why we decided on it. - You know? Right.

403
00:17:00,919 --> 00:17:02,189
That's really cool.

404
00:17:03,229 --> 00:17:04,288
(They enter a barbershop for a new haircut and mindset.)

405
00:17:04,289 --> 00:17:06,458
- How short do you want it? - I want a 6mm buzz cut.

406
00:17:06,459 --> 00:17:07,799
That's pretty short.

407
00:17:09,669 --> 00:17:12,399
Look at his forehead. It's so embarrassing.

408
00:17:12,599 --> 00:17:13,899
Oh, no.

409
00:17:14,269 --> 00:17:15,298
(The tan line is very visible.)

410
00:17:15,299 --> 00:17:16,909
You should've gone to a tanning salon first.

411
00:17:18,339 --> 00:17:20,079
A 6mm buzz cut. Okay.

412
00:17:20,539 --> 00:17:21,679
I'll go right ahead.

413
00:17:23,209 --> 00:17:25,079
- Wait. - What is it?

414
00:17:25,379 --> 00:17:27,019
- Wait. - Yes?

415
00:17:27,349 --> 00:17:28,349
What is it?

416
00:17:28,719 --> 00:17:29,988
Let's go with a 1mm buzz cut.

417
00:17:29,989 --> 00:17:31,119
- A 1mm buzz cut? - Yes.

418
00:17:31,349 --> 00:17:32,549
Let's go with a 1mm buzz cut.

419
00:17:32,619 --> 00:17:33,689
- What? - What?

420
00:17:33,819 --> 00:17:36,288
Monks usually get a 1mm buzz cut.

421
00:17:36,289 --> 00:17:37,328
A 1mm buzz cut?

422
00:17:37,329 --> 00:17:39,629
I got a 1mm buzz cut when I enlisted in the army.

423
00:17:39,759 --> 00:17:40,959
I was so shocked.

424
00:17:41,459 --> 00:17:42,499
A 1mm buzz cut?

425
00:17:43,169 --> 00:17:44,868
I would have to shave his head then.

426
00:17:44,869 --> 00:17:46,899
Let's just do it. I want a new mindset.

427
00:17:47,199 --> 00:17:48,568
I want to start fresh.

428
00:17:48,569 --> 00:17:51,169
- A 1mm buzz cut? Are you sure? - Yes. Let's go with that.

429
00:17:51,809 --> 00:17:53,438
(What's gotten into him?)

430
00:17:53,439 --> 00:17:54,879
- My gosh. - That will be really short.

431
00:17:55,109 --> 00:17:56,179
That sounds better.

432
00:17:56,509 --> 00:17:58,609
He asked for the haircut with...

433
00:17:58,779 --> 00:17:59,948
- A reverent heart? - a reverent heart.

434
00:17:59,949 --> 00:18:02,319
So our journey wasn't over yet.

435
00:18:02,719 --> 00:18:04,888
But we were getting close. It felt so weird.

436
00:18:04,889 --> 00:18:05,918
I bet.

437
00:18:05,919 --> 00:18:07,019
(He's refocusing himself as the end is near.)

438
00:18:08,289 --> 00:18:10,428
(Looking serious)

439
00:18:10,429 --> 00:18:12,559
You can't change your mind now.

440
00:18:12,829 --> 00:18:15,228
- Is this how short you want it? - Yes.

441
00:18:15,229 --> 00:18:16,629
- I could understand him, though. - Do you like it?

442
00:18:16,699 --> 00:18:19,068
- I think I get it too. - It's like being reborn.

443
00:18:19,069 --> 00:18:21,338
- He needed a turning point too. - That was precisely it.

444
00:18:21,339 --> 00:18:22,439
Yes, that's right.

445
00:18:26,739 --> 00:18:28,478
(His hair is getting shorter.)

446
00:18:28,479 --> 00:18:29,879
Gosh, this guy...

447
00:18:31,049 --> 00:18:33,278
- He's getting ready for it too. - Totally.

448
00:18:33,279 --> 00:18:35,249
(His determination to complete the walk is getting stronger.)

449
00:18:36,519 --> 00:18:39,588
(He gets a haircut with a sense of reverence.)

450
00:18:39,589 --> 00:18:41,388
- He looks better with this haircut. - He looks cool.

451
00:18:41,389 --> 00:18:42,659
- He has a beautiful head. - Yes.

452
00:18:43,859 --> 00:18:45,429
This is crazy.

453
00:18:46,329 --> 00:18:48,599
- Should I sit down now? - Sure.

454
00:18:48,759 --> 00:18:49,969
- You should shave your head too. - I...

455
00:18:51,429 --> 00:18:54,898
My hair is pretty long now.

456
00:18:54,899 --> 00:18:56,408
- Okay. - So I want...

457
00:18:56,409 --> 00:18:58,039
this haircut.

458
00:18:58,109 --> 00:18:59,609
- What is it? - What are you showing her?

459
00:18:59,779 --> 00:19:01,738
- Okay. - So I want this haircut.

460
00:19:01,739 --> 00:19:03,178
- Wait. That's Lee Je Hoon. - You showed her Lee Je Hoon?

461
00:19:03,179 --> 00:19:04,209
Hear me out. It's...

462
00:19:04,919 --> 00:19:07,589
(He shows her the hairstyle he wants before the haircut.)

463
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:10,188
- So I want this haircut. - What is it?

464
00:19:10,189 --> 00:19:11,658
- Wait. That's Lee Je Hoon. - You showed her Lee Je Hoon?

465
00:19:11,659 --> 00:19:13,999
Hear me out. It's... What was it called?

466
00:19:14,029 --> 00:19:16,199
- It's called a double haircut. - A double haircut?

467
00:19:16,469 --> 00:19:18,098
- A two-block... What was it? - Isn't that a wolf cut hairstyle?

468
00:19:18,099 --> 00:19:19,368
- A wolf cut! - A wolf cut.

469
00:19:19,369 --> 00:19:21,399
- I hear that's trending these days. - A wolf cut.

470
00:19:21,569 --> 00:19:22,938
- That's... - It's trending now?

471
00:19:22,939 --> 00:19:25,468
- It was trendy 25 years ago. - Or in the early 2000s.

472
00:19:25,469 --> 00:19:26,939
- Really? It's not trendy now? - No.

473
00:19:27,039 --> 00:19:28,338
What are you talking about?

474
00:19:28,339 --> 00:19:29,809
(This is all new to them.)

475
00:19:29,849 --> 00:19:31,808
- Could you cut the side? - Just the side?

476
00:19:31,809 --> 00:19:34,319
My bangs are long too.

477
00:19:34,579 --> 00:19:36,219
I want my bangs to be this short.

478
00:19:37,019 --> 00:19:38,419
This is the overall vibe I want.

479
00:19:39,019 --> 00:19:40,319
I want Woo Seok's haircut.

480
00:19:41,659 --> 00:19:42,789
Do you know Woo Seok?

481
00:19:43,089 --> 00:19:44,229
Well,

482
00:19:44,429 --> 00:19:47,928
we were in the same news articles about four years ago.

483
00:19:47,929 --> 00:19:48,929
News articles?

484
00:19:48,930 --> 00:19:52,198
Reporters published articles saying our era was coming.

485
00:19:52,199 --> 00:19:53,368
They really wrote that?

486
00:19:53,369 --> 00:19:55,668
- Yes. I took many screenshots. - Maybe they made a mistake.

487
00:19:55,669 --> 00:19:57,538
No. There were many news articles about that.

488
00:19:57,539 --> 00:19:59,439
I hear fake news has been spreading a lot.

489
00:20:00,379 --> 00:20:01,709
I love you, Woo Seok.

490
00:20:02,239 --> 00:20:03,449
I'm following your career too.

491
00:20:04,009 --> 00:20:05,978
I believe in your sense of style too.

492
00:20:05,979 --> 00:20:08,849
I saw you cutting his hair. And I knew you were good.

493
00:20:09,579 --> 00:20:10,589
I believe in her.

494
00:20:11,819 --> 00:20:13,188
(She finally starts working on his hair...)

495
00:20:13,189 --> 00:20:14,589
(after a long explanation.)

496
00:20:15,019 --> 00:20:18,059
You look slimmer than I expected. Did you lose a lot of weight?

497
00:20:19,159 --> 00:20:22,299
We walked here all the way from Seoul.

498
00:20:22,759 --> 00:20:25,028
- I started walking from my house. - So you lost a lot of weight.

499
00:20:25,029 --> 00:20:26,298
Right. I lost weight.

500
00:20:26,299 --> 00:20:27,869
(So I'll try wearing Je Hoon's and Woo Seok's hairstyle.)

501
00:20:28,869 --> 00:20:30,469
Don't I look cute in person?

502
00:20:31,739 --> 00:20:32,768
I look cuter in person than on TV, right?

503
00:20:32,769 --> 00:20:34,109
You're fishing for an answer.

504
00:20:34,679 --> 00:20:36,609
- You're not answering me. - You do.

505
00:20:37,749 --> 00:20:39,878
- He's forcing her to answer him. - No.

506
00:20:39,879 --> 00:20:42,319
(Sung Hwan wants to chat.)

507
00:20:42,849 --> 00:20:44,848
(Moving around)

508
00:20:44,849 --> 00:20:45,849
He's doing something.

509
00:20:47,189 --> 00:20:48,388
(Meanwhile, he's done shaving his beard.)

510
00:20:48,389 --> 00:20:50,359
- Oh, my goodness! - He also shaved his beard?

511
00:20:51,159 --> 00:20:53,199
- Oh, my goodness! - He also shaved his beard?

512
00:20:53,559 --> 00:20:54,629
He also has a tan line on his chin.

513
00:20:56,029 --> 00:20:57,428
Right. That's where his beard was.

514
00:20:57,429 --> 00:20:58,429
(Just like his forehead, his beard line is white.)

515
00:20:58,430 --> 00:21:00,199
I thought he was an angel.

516
00:21:00,799 --> 00:21:03,739
I hope someone publishes Hongga-themed emoticons.

517
